+## `enum_next_value`
+
+```cpp
+template <typename E>
+constexpr optional<E> enum_next_value(E value, std::ptrdiff_t n = 1) noexcept;
+
+template <typename E>
+constexpr E enum_next_value_circular(E value, std::ptrdiff_t n = 1) noexcept;
+
+template <typename E>
+constexpr optional<E> enum_prev_value(E value, std::ptrdiff_t n = 1) noexcept;
+
+template <typename E>
+constexpr E enum_prev_value_circular(E value, std::ptrdiff_t n = 1) noexcept;
+```
+
+* Defined in header `<magic_enum/magic_enum_utility.hpp>`
+
+* Moves `n` positions along the enum value sequence, the same order [`enum_values`](#enum_values) returns.
+
+* `n` may be negative, which moves the other way.
+
+* The non-circular forms return an empty `optional` when the destination falls outside the sequence, or when `value` is not an enumerator. The circular forms wrap around instead, and require `value` to be an enumerator.
+
+* Examples
+
+  ```cpp
+  magic_enum::enum_next_value(Color::RED);              // -> optional, value() is Color::BLUE
+  magic_enum::enum_next_value(Color::RED, 2);           // -> optional, value() is Color::GREEN
+  magic_enum::enum_next_value(Color::GREEN);            // -> empty optional, GREEN is last
+  magic_enum::enum_next_value(Color::GREEN, -1);        // -> optional, value() is Color::BLUE
+
+  magic_enum::enum_prev_value(Color::GREEN);            // -> optional, value() is Color::BLUE
+  magic_enum::enum_prev_value(Color::RED);              // -> empty optional, RED is first
+
+  magic_enum::enum_next_value_circular(Color::GREEN);   // -> Color::RED
+  magic_enum::enum_prev_value_circular(Color::RED);     // -> Color::GREEN
+  ```
+
+## `enum_constant`
+
+```cpp
+template <auto V>
+using enum_constant = std::integral_constant<decltype(V), V>;
+```
+
+* Defined in header `<magic_enum/magic_enum.hpp>`
+
+* Carries an enum value as a type, so it can be used where a compile-time constant is needed. It is what [`enum_switch`](#enum_switch) and [`enum_for_each`](#enum_for_each) pass to the lambda, which is why those lambdas take `auto` and read the value back out.
+
+* Examples
+
+  ```cpp
+  magic_enum::enum_constant<Color::GREEN>::value        // -> Color::GREEN
+  magic_enum::enum_constant<Color::GREEN>{}()           // -> Color::GREEN
+
+  magic_enum::enum_for_each<Color>([](auto val) {
+    // val is magic_enum::enum_constant<...>
+    constexpr Color c = decltype(val)::value;
+  });
+  ```
+
