+## `containers::to_array`
+
+```cpp
+template <typename E, typename T, std::size_t N>
+constexpr array<E, T> to_array(T (&a)[N]);
+
+template <typename E, typename T, std::size_t N>
+constexpr array<E, T> to_array(T (&&a)[N]);
+
+template <typename E, typename... Ts>
+constexpr array<E, std::common_type_t<Ts...>> make_array(Ts&&... ts);
+```
+
+* Defined in header `<magic_enum/magic_enum_containers.hpp>`
+
+* Builds a [`containers::array`](#containersarray) from a plain array or from a pack of values. The elements are taken in the order [`enum_values`](#enum_values) returns, so the first element belongs to the first enumerator.
+
+* Both require exactly `enum_count<E>()` elements; a different count does not compile.
+
+* Examples
+
+  ```cpp
+  constexpr auto by_array = magic_enum::containers::to_array<Color>({1, 2, 3});
+  // by_array[Color::RED] -> 1, by_array[Color::BLUE] -> 2, by_array[Color::GREEN] -> 3
+
+  constexpr auto by_pack = magic_enum::containers::make_array<Color>(1, 2, 3);
+  // decltype(by_pack) is magic_enum::containers::array<Color, int>
+  ```
+
